 "description": "T-2234: VLOOKUP/HLOOKUP index just below (and above) an integer. B1:CW1 and A201:A300 hold their own position (1 to 100), so the result is the index Excel used, or #REF! past 100 and #VALUE! below 1. D the index as a formula, E VLOOKUP and F HLOOKUP with the same expression inline, G VLOOKUP reading D (a reference index), H D minus ROUNDDOWN(D,0) to show the double. Rows 80 on: a dense sweep of the cut between 1E-7 and 1E-6 below 2, 100 and 3. Rows 140 on: the cut itself, 2.30E-7 to 2.46E-7 and 2^-22 with tiny offsets. Rows 190 on: 2^-22 (1 + k 2^-12) and (1 + k 2^-20) below 2 and 100.",
